Upstream file: simulation/src/point-to-point/model/qbb-net-device.cc of github.com/aliyun/ns-3-alibabacloud
at commit 3e0c7c1bfbbe9f77890ddcf5e5b9c79fc6dd7437, the ns-3-alibabacloud gitlink of SimAI a57d765.

Cause: QbbNetDevice::Resume(qIndex) reads m_rdmaEQ->GetQp(qIndex) on every PFC RESUME. GetQp returns
RdmaQueuePairGroup::Get(qIndex), which is m_qps[qIndex], the QP at the position of the resumed priority
in the device's QP list. A host with fewer than qIndex + 1 QPs reads past the end of that vector and
dereferences an invalid pointer. rfl-star exits with SIGSEGV, 139, on the first RESUME to a host with
one QP on priority 3.

Reason: the lookup only serves the NVLS test, which can be true for node type 2 alone. Testing the node
type first skips the lookup everywhere else. Every case that did not crash before takes the same branch:
for node type 2 the same lookup and test run as before, and for every other node type the old condition
was always false, so the device went on to DequeueAndTransmit, as it now does directly.

images/ns3/Dockerfile applies this file with git apply right after fetch-sources and fails the build when
it does not apply cleanly.

--- a/simulation/src/point-to-point/model/qbb-net-device.cc
+++ b/simulation/src/point-to-point/model/qbb-net-device.cc
@@ -460,8 +460,7 @@
 		m_paused[qIndex] = false;
 		NS_LOG_INFO("Node " << m_node->GetId() << " dev " << m_ifIndex << " queue " << qIndex <<
 			" resumed at " << Simulator::Now().GetSeconds());
-		Ptr<RdmaQueuePair> lastQp = m_rdmaEQ->GetQp(qIndex);
-		if(lastQp->nvls_enable == 1 && m_node->GetNodeType() == 2) SwitchAsHostSend(); 
+		if (m_node->GetNodeType() == 2 && m_rdmaEQ->GetQp(qIndex)->nvls_enable == 1) SwitchAsHostSend();
 		else DequeueAndTransmit();
 	}
 
